WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.112 --> 00:00:05.132
A masterful effort in storytelling and absolutely
one of the best space dramas around, director

00:00:05.132 --> 00:00:10.852
Ron Howard's Apollo 13 rocked the world when
it premiered in 1995, and has continued spellbinding

00:00:10.852 --> 00:00:12.432
cinema lovers ever since.

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:17.052
The film tells the true tale of the ill-fated
Apollo 13 lunar mission, the Apollo space

00:00:17.052 --> 00:00:21.532
program's third attempt to land on the moon,
which took place in April 1970.

00:00:21.852 --> 00:00:26.672
This Oscar-winning feature stars Tom Hanks,
Kevin Bacon, and Bill Paxton as a trio of

00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:30.632
astronauts who experience a mid-mission explosion
that threatens their lives.

00:00:30.822 --> 00:00:35.632
The unexpected detonation dashed NASA's dream
of additional lunar exploration at the time,

00:00:35.632 --> 00:00:39.632
and it transformed the expedition from one
filled with hope into a race to bring the

00:00:39.632 --> 00:00:41.272
men back to Earth in one piece.

00:00:41.532 --> 00:00:46.052
There's a reason why Apollo 13 is regarded
as Ron Howard's best film yet, and why it

00:00:46.052 --> 00:00:47.792
won all those Academy Awards.

00:00:47.992 --> 00:00:53.022
Netflix subscribers have until June 1st to
discover the magic of Apollo 13 — or else

00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:54.012
they'll be left saying

00:00:54.352 --> 00:00:55.612
"Houston, we have a problem."

00:00:56.572 --> 00:01:02.232
Get into the spooky spirit a season early
with 2009's Friday the 13th, a modern take

00:01:02.232 --> 00:01:04.172
on the horror movie classic from the '80s.

00:01:04.482 --> 00:01:09.092
Supernatural star Jared Padalecki leads the
Friday the 13th refresh, which centers around

00:01:09.092 --> 00:01:12.992
his character, Clay, as he combs through the
woods of the infamous Camp Crystal Lake to

00:01:12.992 --> 00:01:14.192
look for his missing sister.

00:01:14.452 --> 00:01:19.172
He soon discovers the remains of an abandoned
cabin, and later learns that something even

00:01:19.172 --> 00:01:25.552
eerier awaits him in the woodland: the machete-wielding,
hockey mask-wearing serial killer Jason Voorhees.

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:30.412
While many still prefer the original over
this revival, this Friday the 13th is as tense

00:01:30.412 --> 00:01:31.652
as its predecessors.

00:01:31.812 --> 00:01:35.752
It also had significant commercial success,
and is plenty satisfying in its own right.

00:01:36.132 --> 00:01:40.211
Some longtime franchise fans dug the film
so much that they've even placed it in the

00:01:40.212 --> 00:01:43.252
upper tier of their personal best-of-the-series
lists.

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:48.292
Decide where you stand on the original-versus-remake
debate before it disappears from Netflix on

00:01:48.292 --> 00:01:49.292
June 1st.

00:01:50.152 --> 00:01:54.392
Before Will Smith was a big blue Genie in
Disney's live-action Aladdin, he was a bona

00:01:54.392 --> 00:01:57.552
fide leading man who played around in all
sorts of film genres.

00:01:57.652 --> 00:02:02.932
One of his most memorable performances came
in 2007's I Am Legend, in which Smith stars

00:02:02.932 --> 00:02:08.082
as U.S. Army virologist who lives in isolation
after a virus wipes out most of the world's

00:02:08.082 --> 00:02:12.552
population, and which turns the survivors
into deadly creatures known as Darkseekers.

00:02:12.852 --> 00:02:17.492
Aside from all the soul Smith poured into
the film, I Am Legend also tickles the fancies

00:02:17.492 --> 00:02:19.412
of just about every kind of movie fan.

00:02:19.652 --> 00:02:24.892
It's post-apocalyptic, it's sci-fi, it's horror,
it's drama, it's a gritty "what if?"

00:02:24.892 --> 00:02:27.412
story, and at times, it's genuinely funny.

00:02:27.692 --> 00:02:32.232
Those interested in catching it on Netflix
have until June 1st before it's gone forever.

00:02:32.792 --> 00:02:35.212
NO NO NO NO!

00:02:36.906 --> 00:02:41.106
Blending together fictional found footage
and traditional cinematic storytelling, District

00:02:41.106 --> 00:02:45.906
9 takes place in an alternate Johannesburg,
South Africa, and addresses a number of heavy-hitting

00:02:45.906 --> 00:02:47.025
themes in the process.

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:51.726
It tells the story of the South African government
sequestering a group of malnourished aliens

00:02:51.736 --> 00:02:57.546
in an internment camp, featuring Sharlto Copley
playing a bureaucrat working for MNU Department

00:02:57.546 --> 00:02:58.606
of Alien Affairs.

00:02:59.006 --> 00:03:03.466
As his story progresses, the film explores
what it means to be a human, and how segregation

00:03:03.466 --> 00:03:05.246
and xenophobia affects us all.

00:03:05.676 --> 00:03:09.706
Things go sour in the internment camp after
a long period of isolation, and what follows

00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:14.226
is a thrilling and thought-provoking character
drama wrapped up in sci-fi goodness.

00:03:14.446 --> 00:03:18.266
If this sounds like your cup of tea, load
up District 9 before it leaves Netflix on

00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:19.046
June 4th.

00:03:20.466 --> 00:03:24.966
This spacefaring sequel follows the titular
Guardians, offbeat champions of the Marvel

00:03:24.966 --> 00:03:29.746
Cinematic Universe, as they face an attack
from the Sovereign race and its leader Ayesha.

00:03:30.006 --> 00:03:34.026
Because it's the Guardians, it quickly spirals
into a high-stakes adventure to escape imprisonment,

00:03:34.026 --> 00:03:38.896
and along the way, they discover the truth
about Star-Lord's father, the ancient Celestial

00:03:38.896 --> 00:03:40.826
Ego, played by Kurt Russell.

00:03:41.146 --> 00:03:44.786
No spoilers, but he isn't going to win any
Dad of the Year awards.

00:03:45.066 --> 00:03:49.096
Now that the world has entered the post-Avengers:
Endgame timeline, we're all waiting to see

00:03:49.096 --> 00:03:51.526
what Marvel has up its sleeve for Phase 4.

00:03:51.836 --> 00:03:55.846
Guardians of the Galaxy Volume 3 is still
on the distant horizon, so all fans have to

00:03:55.846 --> 00:03:58.966
savor of the franchise for now is the first
Guardians sequel.

00:03:59.086 --> 00:04:00.766
And if you haven't, well…

00:04:00.886 --> 00:04:02.886
You must be so embarassed!

00:04:03.346 --> 00:04:06.646
Don't miss it before it flies off of Netflix
on June 5th.

00:04:08.286 --> 00:04:14.086
Francis Ford Coppola's Vietnam War epic Apocalypse
Now is haunting, visually rousing, and valiant

00:04:14.246 --> 00:04:16.526
one of cinema's most enduring pieces of art.

00:04:16.726 --> 00:04:21.606
Martin Sheen and Marlon Brando lead the film
as U.S. Army special ops officer Captain Benjamin

00:04:21.616 --> 00:04:26.026
L. Willard and the highly feared, heavily
decorated renegade officer Colonel Walter

00:04:26.026 --> 00:04:28.666
E. Kurtz, whom Willard is tasked with taking
out.

00:04:29.276 --> 00:04:34.426
Though Apocalypse Now received mixed reviews
upon its release in 1979, it went on to receive

00:04:34.426 --> 00:04:36.326
eight Academy Award nominations.

00:04:36.586 --> 00:04:42.446
It was later preserved in the Library of Congress'
National Film Registry and designated as "culturally,

00:04:42.446 --> 00:04:44.746
historically or aesthetically significant."

00:04:44.966 --> 00:04:49.806
Apocalypse Now is celebrating its 40th anniversary
this year and will depart from Netflix on

00:04:49.806 --> 00:04:54.586
June 15th, so there truly is no better time
to revisit it, or watch it for the very first

00:04:54.586 --> 00:04:55.086
time.

